[31.029, "o", "Here's what I found for each:\r\n\r\n**SQL query optimization**\r\n- `urn:ai:google.com:skills:bigquery-guidelines` \u2014 SQL optimization, partitioning/clustering, window functions, schema design (Tier 0, no auth, ready)\r\n- `urn:ai:google.com:skills:database-design` \u2014 Cloud SQL/AlloyDB/Spanner: normalization, indexing, connection pooling, migrations (Tier 0, ready)\r\n- `urn:ai:google.com:mcp:alloydb` \u2014 Live Postgres columnar engine queries, cluster scaling (Tier 3, needs `gcloud auth application-default login`)\r\n\r\n**Zero-trust security**\r\n- `urn:ai:google.com:skills:well-architected-security` \u2014 Zero-trust patterns, IAM least-privilege, network perimeters, encryption (Tier 0, ready)\r\n- `urn:ai:google.com:mcp:secret-manager` \u2014 Secret rotation, IAM checks, audit logging (Tier 3, needs GCP auth, has free tier)\r\n- `urn:ai:google.com:mcp:security-command-center` \u2014 Vulnerability findings, CIS compliance, asset inventory (Tier 3, needs GCP auth)\r\n- `urn:ai:google.com:mcp:secops` \u2014 Chronicle SIEM/SOAR threat intel (Tier 4, enterprise)\r\n\r\nThe four Tier 0 skills work offline immediately with no auth. Want me to enable any of them, or onboard the GCP-account MCP servers (secret-manager is free-tier eligible)?\r\n"]
